@Service
public class IdempotentExecutor {
    private final IdempotencyService core;
    public <T> ResponseEntity<String> run(...) {
        try {
            return core.execute(...);
        } catch (DuplicateKeyException ex) {
            return core.replayAfterRace(...);
        }
    }
}
```

Hmm — replayAfterRace needs a transaction? findById read-only, fine without. But it must run AFTER the failed tx rolled back. Since core.execute's @Transactional boundary completes (with rollback) before the exception propagates to the executor, OK.

One concern: DuplicateKeyException thrown during commit (not during insert)? H2 with PK — insert fails immediately at execute time, not deferred. OK.

Another concern: params serialization determinism — the params map built by controller/service. I'll build TreeMap in each endpoint method. Values: strings, numbers, lists. Jackson handles.

Where does requestId validation happen? requireText(requestId, ≤64) — inside execute? Put in executor.run before core.execute? If requestId invalid → 400, shouldn't occupy key — validation before any DB. Put in executor.

